00:29:44.340 --> 00:29:46.680
In a digital world and
with the transformations

00:29:46.680 --> 00:29:50.380
and the changing competitive
landscape, speed to customer

00:29:50.380 --> 00:29:50.880
is key.

00:29:50.880 --> 00:29:52.470
As we build a new
feature, we want

00:29:52.470 --> 00:29:56.530
to get into our customers
hands as quickly as possible.

00:29:56.530 --> 00:29:59.160
But then we start to move into
the real value add for me.

00:29:59.160 --> 00:30:02.370
What I've described as
CI/CD pipelines and stuff

00:30:02.370 --> 00:30:04.820
we've been doing as an
industry for a while.

00:30:04.820 --> 00:30:06.330
But the critical
value add, for me,

00:30:06.330 --> 00:30:08.460
is how we then use
binary authorization

00:30:08.460 --> 00:30:10.920
to automate our governance.

00:30:10.920 --> 00:30:14.580
So as engineers utilize these
pipelines, as an organization

00:30:14.580 --> 00:30:18.120
in terms of our [INAUDIBLE]
for 50,000 employees,

00:30:18.120 --> 00:30:21.780
we can be sure that anybody
there pushing workloads

00:30:21.780 --> 00:30:24.810
to production meet a set
of organizational policies

00:30:24.810 --> 00:30:28.110
that we can enforce,
change, and redesign

00:30:28.110 --> 00:30:31.020
on the fly using this
capability, which gives us

00:30:31.020 --> 00:30:34.350
the ability to do technology
governances as code,

00:30:34.350 --> 00:30:36.140
essentially.

00:30:36.140 --> 00:30:37.480
But that's not enough for us.

00:30:37.480 --> 00:30:39.147
So what we then started
to think through

00:30:39.147 --> 00:30:41.730
is to say, well, if we're
enforcing technology

00:30:41.730 --> 00:30:44.520
governance as code and we're
using these capabilities

00:30:44.520 --> 00:30:46.740
to ensure that we don't
break our appetite

00:30:46.740 --> 00:30:49.982
from an organizational
perspective around tech, well,

00:30:49.982 --> 00:30:52.440
why couldn't we do that with
some of our other requirements

00:30:52.440 --> 00:30:53.770
in terms of our organization?

00:30:53.770 --> 00:30:55.800
What about our
business governance?

00:30:55.800 --> 00:30:58.080
What about our risk
appetite as a bank?

00:30:58.080 --> 00:31:00.540
Can we not start to codify
some of those aspects

00:31:00.540 --> 00:31:03.733
and start to enforce them
via these capabilities?

00:31:03.733 --> 00:31:06.150
Now, that's just something
we're starting to think through

00:31:06.150 --> 00:31:09.450
and starting to adapt, so it's
very much an open question

00:31:09.450 --> 00:31:10.150
mark.

00:31:10.150 --> 00:31:11.775
But that's where
we're heading towards.

00:31:11.775 --> 00:31:13.815
It starting to look
at, as an organization,

00:31:13.815 --> 00:31:14.940
how do we govern ourselves?

00:31:14.940 --> 00:31:17.430
How do we manage
ourselves in terms of risk

00:31:17.430 --> 00:31:20.370
in an automated way and using
something like binary auth

00:31:20.370 --> 00:31:23.160
to enforce that where
we do something,

00:31:23.160 --> 00:31:25.288
it doesn't change
our core values,

00:31:25.288 --> 00:31:27.080
or it doesn't change
our core requirements,

00:31:27.080 --> 00:31:29.070
or it doesn't change
what appetite we

00:31:29.070 --> 00:31:32.220
have as an organization.

00:31:32.220 --> 00:31:35.490
And, again, just
to draw off, as we

00:31:35.490 --> 00:31:38.310
start to progress
[INAUDIBLE],, how do we then

00:31:38.310 --> 00:31:41.665
use this to show compliance
across 30-odd regulators?

00:31:41.665 --> 00:31:43.290
We want to do that
in an automated way.

00:31:43.290 --> 00:31:45.840
We don't want to
be demonstrating

00:31:45.840 --> 00:31:48.150
a set of documents or
a set of requirements

00:31:48.150 --> 00:31:50.700
in a different format for--

00:31:50.700 --> 00:31:53.610
whether it be [INAUDIBLE],,
or [INAUDIBLE] in Singapore,

00:31:53.610 --> 00:31:54.467
or whoever.

00:31:54.467 --> 00:31:56.300
We want to ensure that
they have the ability

00:31:56.300 --> 00:31:57.883
and they have the
confidence that they

00:31:57.883 --> 00:32:01.290
can explore these capabilities
with us and give--

00:32:01.290 --> 00:32:02.790
that we can give
them the confidence

00:32:02.790 --> 00:32:06.020
that we can demonstrate
compliance differently.

00:32:06.020 --> 00:32:09.410
So that's what we're
trying to set out to do

00:32:09.410 --> 00:32:11.630
and why we feel that
there's good business case

00:32:11.630 --> 00:32:14.280
