it's the change process
and you get people on.

00:37:28.430 --> 00:37:30.530
But what we've found
is actually the reason

00:37:30.530 --> 00:37:32.030
to bring people on
the journey early

00:37:32.030 --> 00:37:34.260
is that they started to
get involved in this,

00:37:34.260 --> 00:37:36.020
and they actually really loved
it and enjoyed it, and actually

00:37:36.020 --> 00:37:37.478
started to wanted
to be part of it.

00:37:37.478 --> 00:37:40.100
So we've started to see
a real cultural shift

00:37:40.100 --> 00:37:42.350
and a real coalition around
the organization of people

00:37:42.350 --> 00:37:44.930
wanting to adopt the work
we've been describing.

00:37:44.930 --> 00:37:48.470
So not only spread the message
and bring people on journeys

00:37:48.470 --> 00:37:51.135
to help them embrace the change,
but actually what we've found

00:37:51.135 --> 00:37:53.510
is we've just found helping
hands across the organization

00:37:53.510 --> 00:37:55.660
to make this a reality for us.

00:37:58.350 --> 00:38:00.750
So I think we're at
the closing remarks.

00:38:00.750 --> 00:38:03.110
So the only bit for me to
close with is hopefully

00:38:03.110 --> 00:38:06.950
what you've seen
is ANZ's approach

00:38:06.950 --> 00:38:09.450
to how we want to change
some of the things we do.

00:38:09.450 --> 00:38:12.470
I've described a little bit
of the why we need to do that,

00:38:12.470 --> 00:38:14.090
and hopefully I
brought together how

00:38:14.090 --> 00:38:16.580
we're using some of
Google's capabilities

00:38:16.580 --> 00:38:18.240
to bring that to life.

00:38:18.240 --> 00:38:19.680
And we have two main outcomes.

00:38:19.680 --> 00:38:22.760
One is to make ANZ an amazing
place to work for engineers,

00:38:22.760 --> 00:38:26.518
but two, as quickly as possible,
get consumer value out the door

00:38:26.518 --> 00:38:28.310
and get it into our
hands of our customers.

00:38:28.310 --> 00:38:30.550
And we see the
work I've described

00:38:30.550 --> 00:38:33.410
is a critical aspect to
achieve both those goals as we

00:38:33.410 --> 00:38:35.070
move forward.

00:38:35.070 --> 00:38:36.262
So I'll hand back to Google.

00:38:36.262 --> 00:38:37.970
JUAN SEBASTIAN OVIEDO:
Thank you, Rakesh.

00:38:37.970 --> 00:38:41.720
So as we've seen,
they're applying security

00:38:41.720 --> 00:38:44.570
in coordinating supply
chain has some challenges,

00:38:44.570 --> 00:38:46.070
but also creates
great opportunities

00:38:46.070 --> 00:38:49.520
to both apply that security,
enable your teams to create,

00:38:49.520 --> 00:38:53.600
and to take advantage of that
velocity, and, as a result,

00:38:53.600 --> 00:38:56.030
to provide your customers
with great experiences

00:38:56.030 --> 00:38:58.100
and maintain their trust.

00:38:58.100 --> 00:39:00.230
So here's a summary of
some of the products

00:39:00.230 --> 00:39:02.330
that we talked about today.

